<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lokamahadevi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lokamahadevi was a queen of the Chalukya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-ii">Vikramaditya II</a> in the 8th century. She commissioned the Virupaksha temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pattadakal">Pattadakal</a>, originally called Lokeshvara after her, to commemorate her husband's victory over the Pallavas at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a> around 740. The temple is one of the finest examples of early Dravidian architecture.</p></div>
